.TH LIBRDP-API 7 "2026-07-12" "librdp 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
librdp-api \- public API families for librdp
.SH DESCRIPTION
The public librdp API is declared under
.IR include/librdp .
Applications may include
.B <librdp/librdp.h>
for the full public API or include specific headers for narrower integration.
.SH HEADERS
.TP
.B <librdp/error.h>
Status codes and status-string helper.
.TP
.B <librdp/settings.h>
Settings object, security mode, TLS policy, gateway configuration, feature flags, and redirected device configuration.
.TP
.B <librdp/session.h>
Session lifecycle, event callback registration, connection loop, resize, refresh, display layout, state, surface, and input APIs.
.TP
.B <librdp/event.h>
Event types and callback payload structures.
.TP
.B <librdp/surface.h>
BGRA framebuffer surface allocation, resize, blit, and pixel access.
.TP
.B <librdp/input.h>
Keyboard, mouse, touch, and pen structures and flags.
.TP
.B <librdp/clipboard.h>
Clipboard format, data, file publication, and request APIs.
.TP
.B <librdp/channel.h>
Application-owned dynamic virtual channel send and close APIs.
.TP
.B <librdp/audio.h>
Audio format and audio input response APIs.
.TP
.B <librdp/video.h>
Video capture media and sample response APIs.
.TP
.B <librdp/workspace.h>
Workspace feed discovery and published resource inspection APIs.
.TP
.B <librdp/admin.h>
WinRM administration endpoint configuration and remote session inventory APIs.
.TP
.B <librdp/server.h>
Server listener and accepted-peer lifecycle APIs.
.SH OWNERSHIP
Settings own copied configuration values. Sessions own protocol state and active surfaces. Event payloads are borrowed. Applications must copy event data that must outlive the callback.
.SH ERRORS
Public functions return
.B librdp_status
where failure is possible. Applications should compare against named status constants and use
.BR librdp_status_string ()
for stable diagnostic tokens.
.SH GENERATED REFERENCE
The generated API reference is built from Doxygen comments in public headers. It contains per-symbol pages for functions, structs, enums, macros, callback types, parameters, return codes, ownership, threading, security warnings, and version tags.
.P
Local builds write HTML output to
.IR build/doxygen/html/index.html .
.P
The documentation entry point is
.IR docs/generated-api.md .
.SH USAGE FLOW
A typical application configures
.BR librdp_settings ,
creates a
.BR librdp_session ,
registers an event callback, connects, drives
.BR librdp_session_run_once (),
presents surface invalidations, sends input or feature responses, disconnects, and frees owned objects.
